    "created_at": "2025-04-17T18:58:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-17T18:58:58Z",
    "body": "> Do we need to do something to avoid infinite looping? Fixing the focus can invalidate style/layout, which can necessitate fixing the focus.\n\nThere's already the resize observer depth thing that breaks the infinite loop, we should reuse that.\nI think the only clean thing to do would be to put the focus fixup inside that same loop. Really any side-effect of style that can trigger a synchronous script should be inside that loop, and we should try to make future ones as async as possible to avoid this issue.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
